# Pairs with RevertReturns, under the fairness Spec asserts (issue #4441 F9).
# A retried revert that finds the alias already back on the previous copy
# returns without redoing the redirect fix-up, so a revert that crashed
# between its swap and that fix-up never returns.
MODULE: RevertReturnsRetryStopsAfterSwap
TARGET: RevertReturns
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a retried revert never resumes the redirect fix-up after a crash
PERTURBS: Retry

--- FIND
               [] alias = "prev" -> "reverting"
--- REPLACE
               \* MUTATION: the retry stays failed once the alias is back.
               [] alias = "prev" -> "revertFailed"
--- END